wine spectator magazine just released  its winners in their annual restaurant  awards and we told you that 59 local  spots made the list and five received  top honors named grand award winners  joining us this morning to talk about it  cassia shifter wine spectators associate  tasting coordinator and the director of  the restaurant awards  cassia thanks for being here this  morning talk to me about the las vegas  restaurants that made the list and what  made these particular spots stand out  yeah of course thank you for having me  good morning  there are as you said 59 winners in las  vegas and five of them are our grand  award winners  and we have three levels of award the  award of excellence best of award of  excellence and the grand award which is  our top highest honor only 97  restaurants in the world currently hold  it  um what we look for there and how they  caught our eye is you know generally a  wine list that has over a thousand  selection which is a huge a huge number  a lot of diversity both in terms of  where the wines are from uh vintages  producer pretty much everything  has to have great presentation  all the correct information um  and just sort of go above and beyond the  extra mile in terms of service educating  their staff who can then educate the  diners  because our goal is just to make sure  everyone feels comfortable going to a  restaurant ordering a bottle of wine  that they love ah and that's so  important too you know obviously the  sommeliers help with that so i'm  guessing when you're going through these  wines are you looking at the food items  that are served as well and to see if  there's some kind of connection or good  pairing options  absolutely  it's definitely not the end all and be  all but you know if you're going to a  sushi restaurant and they only have  cabernet sauvignon on the menu i feel  like that's a little bit limiting and in  the same vein you know a steakhouse that  only has white wine might be a little  odd pairing um  but for the most part  you know as long as it's a really good  wine less and it does fit the vibe of  the restaurant the theme of the  restaurant the cuisine  you know that's the more important part  of  the awards are you know having that put  together wine list with great selections  well vegas knows how to do it i'll tell  you that really quick before i let you  go for the average wine consumer  you know is it about the vineyard and  the location or is it about the brand  what should we be looking looking at  honestly it's really about personal  preference and you know people ask me  all the time how do i learn about wine  how do i get to know  all the important things  i i really think the most important  thing is just knowing what you like  knowing  you know what you don't like  knowing what's in your correct price  range and being able to order that  confidently is more important to me i  think than  you know knowing you know the grand cru  vineyards of burgundy and such  all good information cassia thank you so  much for joining us this morning as we  get ready for our  wine tasting weekend i suppose  have a great day thank you
 

